      "message": "`slugify` now takes an optional `max_length`, and it drops whole trailing words instead of cutting one in half. All 3 tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass, including the new one.\n\nThe change is in `slug/core.py`:\n- With no `max_length`, behaviour is unchanged.\n- If the slug is already within the limit, it is returned as is.\n- Otherwise it is cut at the last `-` that fits, so `\"alpha beta gamma\"` with `max_length=10` gives `\"alpha-beta\"`.\n- If the first word alone is longer than the limit, it returns `\"\"`. I chose this over cutting the word, since you asked that words never be cut. Say if you'd rather it fall back to a hard cut.\n- A negative `max_length` raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe test is `test_max_length_drops_whole_words` in `tests/test_core.py`. It checks the boundary cases and the empty-result case.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
